{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/254489-uncle-horus-wants-you","id":254489,"title":"Uncle Horus Wants You!!!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-11T11:44:43-07:00","id":254489,"title":"Uncle Horus Wants You!!!","content":"Hey all. You may remember that my game question in the VtM forum suggests that I'm in a game of vampire, making &quot;I hope this never happens&quot; plans to replace my character if a particular gambit should not pay off like I'm hoping. Now, I brought up the replacement I was going for; an Assamie Vizier, but my Storyteller hit me with an idea that I think I'd actually like to try out.<br /> <br /> Basically, he's giving me the option of bringing a Mummy to this elder Vampire chronicle. This will be using most of the mechanics from Mummy 2nd Edition, but the Hekau mechanics from Revised.<br /> <br /> I've never played a Mummy before, so I wanted to get some advice on building her effectively. What are skills/abilities/Hekau I should definitely go for, and which should I avoid like a bad cliche? What's the most effective role for mummies, especially given that she's going undercover as a vampire fledgling? Gimme some advice and recommendations, you lovely crazy White Wolf players, you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T12:02:45-07:00","id":257471,"title":"","content":"Awwwwww. No love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T14:36:41-07:00","id":257605,"title":"","content":"Going with the MtR Hekau and 2nd ed Mummies? Celestial Hekau is rather strong against Vampires, being able to amongst other things inflict daylight penalties to Vamps, while either Amulets or Alchemy is recommended to blend in with the Vampires as both of the aforementioned can give you physicality beyond that of humans as well as supernatural social abilities through boosting your social stats, Alchemy even gives you Presence like abilities through your potions and incenses etc. So those can help you in your Masquerade. Necromancy is always useful especially in matters of death and undeath, specifically it helps in finding out who is a Vampire and who is not, Judging the Soul of a Vampire tends to reveal their Blood Lust quite clearly, and it does give the Mummy a source of Aggravated Damage in hand to hand combat though in a manner that is both obvious and un-vampire like, still useful to have when feces hit's the fan. Best of all though in general is perhaps Nomenclature which can give you both Healing and damage, the latter even in most gruesome manner as you designate an organ or body part for destruction.<br /> <br /> So in short if you intend to Masquerade as a Vampire as a first priority I would suggest either Amulets or Alchemy, first has the advantage of long term effect the second has the advantage of being able to do a considerable amount of things that help in playing vampire like manipulating emotions, healing faster (through salves or potions), and temporarily boosting attributes. Used craftily enough no one will even notice where you gained those boosts, consider carefully whether to make something as a potion, salve or something else.<br /> Then after one or the other of the above I would go for either Celestial or Necromancy for intelligence gathering and defense.<br /> <br /> Of course if oyur ST allows you to go straight for Nomenclature then take that as a first Priority and then follow the instructions above.<br /> <br /> These are just my humble opinions of course, YMMV, and given with the idea that going b 2nd ed rules and revised Hekau means you will have no Balance stat holding you back in regards to access to Hekau.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}